  user_input {
    user_response: "You are a senior frontend architect and senior React/TypeScript engineer.\n\nI have uploaded multiple screenshots of my **MPLADS Sentinel** UI created in Google Stitch.\n\nBuild a **highly responsive, highly interactive, production-quality frontend** based on these screenshots.\n\nThe screenshots are the PRIMARY visual reference. Preserve their design, layout, spacing, typography, colors, navigation structure and visual hierarchy, while making every reasonable UI element functional.\n\n==================================================\nPROJECT\n=======\n\nMPLADS Sentinel is an AI-powered MPLADS monitoring and transparency platform.\n\nThe future system will work with real MPLADS project data and provide:\n\n* Project monitoring\n* Financial analysis\n* Delay detection\n* Anomaly detection\n* Risk scoring\n* Duplicate/similar project detection\n* Geographic analysis\n* Reports\n* AI-powered explanations\n* RAG-based assistance using official MPLADS documents\n\nFor THIS TASK, build the complete interactive frontend.\n\nDo NOT implement the real ML model, RAG backend or production database yet.\n\nUse realistic mock data and create clean interfaces so that real APIs can be connected later.\n\n==================================================\nCORE REQUIREMENT \342\200\224 EVERYTHING SHOULD FEEL FUNCTIONAL\n====================================================\n\nDo NOT create a static prototype.\n\nWhenever the user performs an action, the interface should respond appropriately.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Clicking a button should do something.\n* Clicking a project should open/navigate to its details.\n* Searching should filter results.\n* Filters should update the displayed data.\n* Sorting should work.\n* Pagination should work.\n* Tabs should switch content.\n* Dropdowns should work.\n* Modals should open and close.\n* Forms should validate.\n* Save buttons should update state.\n* Reset buttons should reset state.\n* Toggle switches should work.\n* Notifications should appear when appropriate.\n* Charts should respond to selections where reasonable.\n* Sidebar navigation should work.\n* Mobile navigation should work.\n* Back buttons should work.\n* Export/download buttons should provide a realistic frontend response.\n* AI Assistant should behave like a functional mock chat.\n* Loading states should exist.\n* Empty states should exist.\n* Error states should exist.\n\nDo not use dead buttons unless there is absolutely no meaningful frontend behavior possible.\n\n==================================================\nRESPONSIVE DESIGN\n=================\n\nThis is VERY IMPORTANT.\n\nThe website must be genuinely responsive, NOT simply desktop UI scaled down.\n\nSupport:\n\n* Large desktop\n* Desktop\n* Laptop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n* Small mobile\n\nUse responsive Tailwind breakpoints.\n\nDesktop:\n\n* Persistent sidebar where appropriate\n* Multi-column layouts\n* Full data tables\n* Charts and analytics\n\nTablet:\n\n* Adaptive grid\n* Collapsible navigation\n* Responsive tables\n* Appropriate card stacking\n\nMobile:\n\n* Hamburger navigation\n* Bottom/compact actions where appropriate\n* Cards instead of overly wide tables\n* Horizontal scrolling only when genuinely necessary\n* Responsive charts\n* Touch-friendly controls\n* Proper spacing\n* No content overflowing the screen\n\nTest every page at multiple viewport sizes.\n\nNever allow:\n\n* horizontal page overflow\n* overlapping components\n* text clipping\n* buttons going outside containers\n* charts being cut off\n* broken tables\n\n==================================================\nTECH STACK\n==========\n\nUse:\n\nReact\nTypeScript\nVite\nTailwind CSS\nReact Router\nRecharts\nLucide React\n\nUse modern React patterns.\n\nCreate reusable components.\n\n==================================================\nROUTES\n======\n\nImplement:\n\n/dashboard\n/projects\n/projects/:id\n/risk-analysis\n/map\n/ai-assistant\n/reports\n/settings\n\nNavigation between all pages must work.\n\nUse React Router properly.\n\n==================================================\nGLOBAL APPLICATION BEHAVIOR\n===========================\n\nCreate:\n\n* Global layout\n* Responsive sidebar\n* Responsive top navigation\n* Breadcrumbs where appropriate\n* Notification system\n* Toast feedback\n* Loading states\n* Empty states\n* Error states\n* Confirmation dialogs\n* Search\n* Theme-ready structure\n\nMaintain application state cleanly.\n\nDo not put everything in App.tsx.\n\n==================================================\nMOCK DATA ARCHITECTURE\n======================\n\nCreate:\n\nsrc/\ncomponents/\npages/\nlayouts/\ndata/\ntypes/\nhooks/\nutils/\n\nKeep mock data separate from UI.\n\nCreate realistic MPLADS project records.\n\nExample fields:\n\nprojectId\nmpName\nstate\ndistrict\nconstituency\nworkDescription\ncategory\nrecommendedAmount\nfinalAmount\ntotalPaid\nstatus\nrecommendationDate\nsanctionDate\ncompletedDate\nimplementingAgency\nriskScore\nriskLevel\nlatitude\nlongitude\n\nCreate enough mock records to demonstrate:\n\n* search\n* filtering\n* sorting\n* pagination\n* charts\n* risk analysis\n* project details\n\n==================================================\nDASHBOARD\n=========\n\nRecreate the uploaded Stitch dashboard.\n\nMake dashboard widgets interactive.\n\nExamples:\n\nSTAT CARDS\n\n* Total Projects\n* Total Recommended Amount\n* Total Paid\n* Completed Projects\n* Pending Projects\n* High Risk Projects\n\nAllow relevant cards to navigate to filtered project views.\n\nCHARTS\n\nImplement functional Recharts charts.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Project status distribution\n* Expenditure trend\n* State-wise project distribution\n* Risk distribution\n* Category distribution\n\nWhere appropriate, clicking chart elements should filter/navigate to relevant projects.\n\nFILTERS\n\nImplement:\n\n* State\n* District\n* Constituency\n* Status\n* Risk level\n* Category\n* Date range\n\nDashboard data should update according to filters.\n\n==================================================\nPROJECTS PAGE\n=============\n\nCreate a highly functional project management/exploration page.\n\nFeatures:\n\n1. Search\n2. Multi-filter\n3. Sorting\n4. Pagination\n5. Column handling where appropriate\n6. Project selection\n7. Project details navigation\n8. Clear filters\n9. Result count\n10. Loading state\n11. Empty state\n\nSearch across:\n\n* Project ID\n* MP name\n* State\n* District\n* Constituency\n* Work description\n* Implementing agency\n\nSorting:\n\n* Recommended amount\n* Total paid\n* Risk score\n* Recommendation date\n* Completion date\n\nClicking a project should navigate to:\n\n/projects/:id\n\n==================================================\nPROJECT DETAILS\n===============\n\nCreate a detailed project page.\n\nShow:\n\n* Project ID\n* MP\n* State\n* District\n* Constituency\n* Work description\n* Category\n* Implementing agency\n* Recommended amount\n* Final amount\n* Total paid\n* Status\n* Important dates\n* Risk score\n\nCreate:\n\n* Project timeline\n* Financial summary\n* Risk analysis section\n* Activity/history section\n\nInteractive actions:\n\n* Back to projects\n* Bookmark/watch project\n* Share project\n* Print\n* Download report\n* Flag for review\n\nFor actions that don\'t have backend functionality yet, provide realistic frontend behavior and feedback.\n\n==================================================\nRISK ANALYSIS\n=============\n\nCreate an interactive risk analysis dashboard.\n\nShow:\n\n* Overall risk distribution\n* High-risk projects\n* Medium-risk projects\n* Low-risk projects\n* Risk categories\n* Financial anomalies\n* Delay anomalies\n* Duplicate/similarity indicators\n\nFilters must work.\n\nRisk score should be visually clear.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nNever state that a project is definitely fraudulent.\n\nUse terminology such as:\n\n\"High Risk\"\n\"Anomaly Detected\"\n\"Requires Verification\"\n\"Unusual Pattern\"\n\nCreate a project risk details interaction.\n\n==================================================\nMAP\n===\n\nCreate an interactive geographic monitoring page.\n\nIf a real map library is not necessary at this stage, create a high-quality interactive map component/placeholder matching the Stitch design.\n\nIt should support frontend interactions such as:\n\n* State selection\n* Project selection\n* Risk filtering\n* Location information\n* Project count\n* Risk level\n\nPrepare the architecture so a real GIS/map API can be integrated later.\n\n==================================================\nAI ASSISTANT\n============\n\nCreate a fully interactive mock AI Assistant.\n\nFeatures:\n\n* Chat input\n* Send button\n* Enter-to-send\n* Conversation history\n* Suggested questions\n* Clear conversation\n* Loading/typing indicator\n* Mock AI responses\n* Source/citation placeholders\n* Copy response\n* Retry response\n\nExample questions:\n\n\"Show me high-risk projects in Maharashtra.\"\n\n\"Which constituencies have low utilization?\"\n\n\"Why was this project flagged?\"\n\n\"Show delayed projects.\"\n\nThe assistant should return realistic mock responses based on the mock project data where possible.\n\nDo not connect a real LLM yet.\n\n==================================================\nREPORTS\n=======\n\nCreate an interactive Reports page.\n\nFeatures:\n\n* Report categories\n* Filters\n* Date range\n* State/district selection\n* Preview report\n* Generate report\n* Download button\n* Recent reports\n* Report status\n\nFor now, report generation can be simulated on the frontend.\n\nShow loading/progress feedback.\n\n==================================================\nSETTINGS\n========\n\nCreate functional settings sections.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Profile\n* Notifications\n* Dashboard preferences\n* Display preferences\n* Data refresh preferences\n\nUse real frontend state.\n\nSave buttons should show confirmation.\n\nReset buttons should restore defaults.\n\n==================================================\nINTERACTION DESIGN\n==================\n\nUse polished interactions:\n\n* Hover states\n* Focus states\n* Active states\n* Disabled states\n* Loading states\n* Toast notifications\n* Modal transitions\n* Dropdown transitions\n* Skeleton loading\n* Tooltips where useful\n\nKeep animations subtle and professional.\n\nDo not over-animate the government analytics interface.\n\n==================================================\nACCESSIBILITY\n=============\n\nFollow good accessibility practices.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Semantic HTML\n* Keyboard navigation\n* Visible focus states\n* Accessible labels\n* Proper button elements\n* ARIA attributes where required\n* Good contrast\n* Touch-friendly controls\n\n==================================================\nVISUAL DESIGN\n=============\n\nThe uploaded Stitch screenshots are the primary visual reference.\n\nDo NOT turn this into a generic AI dashboard.\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Purple/blue AI gradients\n* Gradient blobs\n* Excessive glassmorphism\n* Excessive rounded cards\n* Huge hero sections\n* Excessive shadows\n* Random emojis\n* Decorative elements that reduce data readability\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* Government-grade professionalism\n* Trust\n* Data readability\n* Clear hierarchy\n* Clean typography\n* Consistent spacing\n* Strong information architecture\n* Responsive behavior\n\n==================================================\nFUTURE BACKEND COMPATIBILITY\n============================\n\nThe frontend will eventually connect to:\n\nCSV\n\342\206\223\nSupabase PostgreSQL\n\342\206\223\nBackend/API\n\342\206\223\nML anomaly detection\n\342\206\223\nRisk scoring\n\342\206\223\nRAG/AI\n\342\206\223\nFrontend\n\nTherefore:\n\n* Keep API/data access separate from components.\n* Create service functions/interfaces where appropriate.\n* Do not hardcode data inside components.\n* Use TypeScript interfaces.\n* Make it easy to replace mock data with API calls later.\n\nExample future structure:\n\nsrc/services/\nprojectService.ts\ndashboardService.ts\nriskService.ts\nreportService.ts\naiService.ts\n\nFor now these services may use mock data.\n\n==================================================\nPERFORMANCE\n===========\n\nThe application must remain responsive even with thousands of mock project records.\n\nAvoid unnecessary re-renders.\n\nUse efficient filtering and pagination.\n\nDo not load huge unnecessary components repeatedly.\n\n==================================================\nERROR HANDLING\n==============\n\nCreate realistic:\n\n* Loading state\n* Empty state\n* Error state\n* Retry action\n\nDo not allow an error to break the entire application.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL QUALITY CHECK\n===================\n\nBefore finishing, verify:\n\n1. All routes work.\n2. Navigation works.\n3. Mobile navigation works.\n4. Search works.\n5. Filters work.\n6. Sorting works.\n7. Pagination works.\n8. Project details work.\n9. Charts render.\n10. Interactive dashboard works.\n11. Risk analysis interactions work.\n12. AI Assistant works as a mock interface.\n13. Report interactions work.\n14. Settings interactions work.\n15. Buttons have meaningful behavior.\n16. Loading states exist.\n17. Empty states exist.\n18. Error states exist.\n19. No horizontal overflow.\n20. No TypeScript errors.\n21. No broken imports.\n22. No console errors.\n23. UI closely matches the uploaded Stitch screenshots.\n24. Desktop layout is polished.\n25. Mobile layout is genuinely responsive.\n\nDo not stop at generating a visual mockup.\n\nBuild a complete, interactive frontend application that feels like a real working product.\n\nThe backend, Supabase, real MPLADS CSV, ML anomaly detection and RAG will be integrated later.\n\n"
    items {
      text: "You are a senior frontend architect and senior React/TypeScript engineer.\n\nI have uploaded multiple screenshots of my **MPLADS Sentinel** UI created in Google Stitch.\n\nBuild a **highly responsive, highly interactive, production-quality frontend** based on these screenshots.\n\nThe screenshots are the PRIMARY visual reference. Preserve their design, layout, spacing, typography, colors, navigation structure and visual hierarchy, while making every reasonable UI element functional.\n\n==================================================\nPROJECT\n=======\n\nMPLADS Sentinel is an AI-powered MPLADS monitoring and transparency platform.\n\nThe future system will work with real MPLADS project data and provide:\n\n* Project monitoring\n* Financial analysis\n* Delay detection\n* Anomaly detection\n* Risk scoring\n* Duplicate/similar project detection\n* Geographic analysis\n* Reports\n* AI-powered explanations\n* RAG-based assistance using official MPLADS documents\n\nFor THIS TASK, build the complete interactive frontend.\n\nDo NOT implement the real ML model, RAG backend or production database yet.\n\nUse realistic mock data and create clean interfaces so that real APIs can be connected later.\n\n==================================================\nCORE REQUIREMENT \342\200\224 EVERYTHING SHOULD FEEL FUNCTIONAL\n====================================================\n\nDo NOT create a static prototype.\n\nWhenever the user performs an action, the interface should respond appropriately.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Clicking a button should do something.\n* Clicking a project should open/navigate to its details.\n* Searching should filter results.\n* Filters should update the displayed data.\n* Sorting should work.\n* Pagination should work.\n* Tabs should switch content.\n* Dropdowns should work.\n* Modals should open and close.\n* Forms should validate.\n* Save buttons should update state.\n* Reset buttons should reset state.\n* Toggle switches should work.\n* Notifications should appear when appropriate.\n* Charts should respond to selections where reasonable.\n* Sidebar navigation should work.\n* Mobile navigation should work.\n* Back buttons should work.\n* Export/download buttons should provide a realistic frontend response.\n* AI Assistant should behave like a functional mock chat.\n* Loading states should exist.\n* Empty states should exist.\n* Error states should exist.\n\nDo not use dead buttons unless there is absolutely no meaningful frontend behavior possible.\n\n==================================================\nRESPONSIVE DESIGN\n=================\n\nThis is VERY IMPORTANT.\n\nThe website must be genuinely responsive, NOT simply desktop UI scaled down.\n\nSupport:\n\n* Large desktop\n* Desktop\n* Laptop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n* Small mobile\n\nUse responsive Tailwind breakpoints.\n\nDesktop:\n\n* Persistent sidebar where appropriate\n* Multi-column layouts\n* Full data tables\n* Charts and analytics\n\nTablet:\n\n* Adaptive grid\n* Collapsible navigation\n* Responsive tables\n* Appropriate card stacking\n\nMobile:\n\n* Hamburger navigation\n* Bottom/compact actions where appropriate\n* Cards instead of overly wide tables\n* Horizontal scrolling only when genuinely necessary\n* Responsive charts\n* Touch-friendly controls\n* Proper spacing\n* No content overflowing the screen\n\nTest every page at multiple viewport sizes.\n\nNever allow:\n\n* horizontal page overflow\n* overlapping components\n* text clipping\n* buttons going outside containers\n* charts being cut off\n* broken tables\n\n==================================================\nTECH STACK\n==========\n\nUse:\n\nReact\nTypeScript\nVite\nTailwind CSS\nReact Router\nRecharts\nLucide React\n\nUse modern React patterns.\n\nCreate reusable components.\n\n==================================================\nROUTES\n======\n\nImplement:\n\n/dashboard\n/projects\n/projects/:id\n/risk-analysis\n/map\n/ai-assistant\n/reports\n/settings\n\nNavigation between all pages must work.\n\nUse React Router properly.\n\n==================================================\nGLOBAL APPLICATION BEHAVIOR\n===========================\n\nCreate:\n\n* Global layout\n* Responsive sidebar\n* Responsive top navigation\n* Breadcrumbs where appropriate\n* Notification system\n* Toast feedback\n* Loading states\n* Empty states\n* Error states\n* Confirmation dialogs\n* Search\n* Theme-ready structure\n\nMaintain application state cleanly.\n\nDo not put everything in App.tsx.\n\n==================================================\nMOCK DATA ARCHITECTURE\n======================\n\nCreate:\n\nsrc/\ncomponents/\npages/\nlayouts/\ndata/\ntypes/\nhooks/\nutils/\n\nKeep mock data separate from UI.\n\nCreate realistic MPLADS project records.\n\nExample fields:\n\nprojectId\nmpName\nstate\ndistrict\nconstituency\nworkDescription\ncategory\nrecommendedAmount\nfinalAmount\ntotalPaid\nstatus\nrecommendationDate\nsanctionDate\ncompletedDate\nimplementingAgency\nriskScore\nriskLevel\nlatitude\nlongitude\n\nCreate enough mock records to demonstrate:\n\n* search\n* filtering\n* sorting\n* pagination\n* charts\n* risk analysis\n* project details\n\n==================================================\nDASHBOARD\n=========\n\nRecreate the uploaded Stitch dashboard.\n\nMake dashboard widgets interactive.\n\nExamples:\n\nSTAT CARDS\n\n* Total Projects\n* Total Recommended Amount\n* Total Paid\n* Completed Projects\n* Pending Projects\n* High Risk Projects\n\nAllow relevant cards to navigate to filtered project views.\n\nCHARTS\n\nImplement functional Recharts charts.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Project status distribution\n* Expenditure trend\n* State-wise project distribution\n* Risk distribution\n* Category distribution\n\nWhere appropriate, clicking chart elements should filter/navigate to relevant projects.\n\nFILTERS\n\nImplement:\n\n* State\n* District\n* Constituency\n* Status\n* Risk level\n* Category\n* Date range\n\nDashboard data should update according to filters.\n\n==================================================\nPROJECTS PAGE\n=============\n\nCreate a highly functional project management/exploration page.\n\nFeatures:\n\n1. Search\n2. Multi-filter\n3. Sorting\n4. Pagination\n5. Column handling where appropriate\n6. Project selection\n7. Project details navigation\n8. Clear filters\n9. Result count\n10. Loading state\n11. Empty state\n\nSearch across:\n\n* Project ID\n* MP name\n* State\n* District\n* Constituency\n* Work description\n* Implementing agency\n\nSorting:\n\n* Recommended amount\n* Total paid\n* Risk score\n* Recommendation date\n* Completion date\n\nClicking a project should navigate to:\n\n/projects/:id\n\n==================================================\nPROJECT DETAILS\n===============\n\nCreate a detailed project page.\n\nShow:\n\n* Project ID\n* MP\n* State\n* District\n* Constituency\n* Work description\n* Category\n* Implementing agency\n* Recommended amount\n* Final amount\n* Total paid\n* Status\n* Important dates\n* Risk score\n\nCreate:\n\n* Project timeline\n* Financial summary\n* Risk analysis section\n* Activity/history section\n\nInteractive actions:\n\n* Back to projects\n* Bookmark/watch project\n* Share project\n* Print\n* Download report\n* Flag for review\n\nFor actions that don\'t have backend functionality yet, provide realistic frontend behavior and feedback.\n\n==================================================\nRISK ANALYSIS\n=============\n\nCreate an interactive risk analysis dashboard.\n\nShow:\n\n* Overall risk distribution\n* High-risk projects\n* Medium-risk projects\n* Low-risk projects\n* Risk categories\n* Financial anomalies\n* Delay anomalies\n* Duplicate/similarity indicators\n\nFilters must work.\n\nRisk score should be visually clear.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nNever state that a project is definitely fraudulent.\n\nUse terminology such as:\n\n\"High Risk\"\n\"Anomaly Detected\"\n\"Requires Verification\"\n\"Unusual Pattern\"\n\nCreate a project risk details interaction.\n\n==================================================\nMAP\n===\n\nCreate an interactive geographic monitoring page.\n\nIf a real map library is not necessary at this stage, create a high-quality interactive map component/placeholder matching the Stitch design.\n\nIt should support frontend interactions such as:\n\n* State selection\n* Project selection\n* Risk filtering\n* Location information\n* Project count\n* Risk level\n\nPrepare the architecture so a real GIS/map API can be integrated later.\n\n==================================================\nAI ASSISTANT\n============\n\nCreate a fully interactive mock AI Assistant.\n\nFeatures:\n\n* Chat input\n* Send button\n* Enter-to-send\n* Conversation history\n* Suggested questions\n* Clear conversation\n* Loading/typing indicator\n* Mock AI responses\n* Source/citation placeholders\n* Copy response\n* Retry response\n\nExample questions:\n\n\"Show me high-risk projects in Maharashtra.\"\n\n\"Which constituencies have low utilization?\"\n\n\"Why was this project flagged?\"\n\n\"Show delayed projects.\"\n\nThe assistant should return realistic mock responses based on the mock project data where possible.\n\nDo not connect a real LLM yet.\n\n==================================================\nREPORTS\n=======\n\nCreate an interactive Reports page.\n\nFeatures:\n\n* Report categories\n* Filters\n* Date range\n* State/district selection\n* Preview report\n* Generate report\n* Download button\n* Recent reports\n* Report status\n\nFor now, report generation can be simulated on the frontend.\n\nShow loading/progress feedback.\n\n==================================================\nSETTINGS\n========\n\nCreate functional settings sections.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Profile\n* Notifications\n* Dashboard preferences\n* Display preferences\n* Data refresh preferences\n\nUse real frontend state.\n\nSave buttons should show confirmation.\n\nReset buttons should restore defaults.\n\n==================================================\nINTERACTION DESIGN\n==================\n\nUse polished interactions:\n\n* Hover states\n* Focus states\n* Active states\n* Disabled states\n* Loading states\n* Toast notifications\n* Modal transitions\n* Dropdown transitions\n* Skeleton loading\n* Tooltips where useful\n\nKeep animations subtle and professional.\n\nDo not over-animate the government analytics interface.\n\n==================================================\nACCESSIBILITY\n=============\n\nFollow good accessibility practices.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Semantic HTML\n* Keyboard navigation\n* Visible focus states\n* Accessible labels\n* Proper button elements\n* ARIA attributes where required\n* Good contrast\n* Touch-friendly controls\n\n==================================================\nVISUAL DESIGN\n=============\n\nThe uploaded Stitch screenshots are the primary visual reference.\n\nDo NOT turn this into a generic AI dashboard.\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Purple/blue AI gradients\n* Gradient blobs\n* Excessive glassmorphism\n* Excessive rounded cards\n* Huge hero sections\n* Excessive shadows\n* Random emojis\n* Decorative elements that reduce data readability\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* Government-grade professionalism\n* Trust\n* Data readability\n* Clear hierarchy\n* Clean typography\n* Consistent spacing\n* Strong information architecture\n* Responsive behavior\n\n==================================================\nFUTURE BACKEND COMPATIBILITY\n============================\n\nThe frontend will eventually connect to:\n\nCSV\n\342\206\223\nSupabase PostgreSQL\n\342\206\223\nBackend/API\n\342\206\223\nML anomaly detection\n\342\206\223\nRisk scoring\n\342\206\223\nRAG/AI\n\342\206\223\nFrontend\n\nTherefore:\n\n* Keep API/data access separate from components.\n* Create service functions/interfaces where appropriate.\n* Do not hardcode data inside components.\n* Use TypeScript interfaces.\n* Make it easy to replace mock data with API calls later.\n\nExample future structure:\n\nsrc/services/\nprojectService.ts\ndashboardService.ts\nriskService.ts\nreportService.ts\naiService.ts\n\nFor now these services may use mock data.\n\n==================================================\nPERFORMANCE\n===========\n\nThe application must remain responsive even with thousands of mock project records.\n\nAvoid unnecessary re-renders.\n\nUse efficient filtering and pagination.\n\nDo not load huge unnecessary components repeatedly.\n\n==================================================\nERROR HANDLING\n==============\n\nCreate realistic:\n\n* Loading state\n* Empty state\n* Error state\n* Retry action\n\nDo not allow an error to break the entire application.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL QUALITY CHECK\n===================\n\nBefore finishing, verify:\n\n1. All routes work.\n2. Navigation works.\n3. Mobile navigation works.\n4. Search works.\n5. Filters work.\n6. Sorting works.\n7. Pagination works.\n8. Project details work.\n9. Charts render.\n10. Interactive dashboard works.\n11. Risk analysis interactions work.\n12. AI Assistant works as a mock interface.\n13. Report interactions work.\n14. Settings interactions work.\n15. Buttons have meaningful behavior.\n16. Loading states exist.\n17. Empty states exist.\n18. Error states exist.\n19. No horizontal overflow.\n20. No TypeScript errors.\n21. No broken imports.\n22. No console errors.\n23. UI closely matches the uploaded Stitch screenshots.\n24. Desktop layout is polished.\n25. Mobile layout is genuinely responsive.\n\nDo not stop at generating a visual mockup.\n\nBuild a complete, interactive frontend application that feels like a real working product.\n\nThe backend, Supabase, real MPLADS CSV, ML anomaly detection and RAG will be integrated later.\n\n"
    }
