  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Project Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the application. I\'ve begun to define the required folders and files, like `src/types/index.ts`. This file will hold the TypeScript types and interfaces for the project, including Project, Status, RiskLevel, Sector, TimelineMilestone, RiskFactor, AuditLog, and Evidence. I\'m aiming for a well-organized and typed foundation for the application.\n\n\n**Establishing Data Layer**\n\nI\'ve been working on populating the mock data files. I\'ve focused on `mockProjects.ts`, which now contains comprehensive MPLADS project data across Indian states with real-world information. I\'m also developing `mockRiskClusters.ts` to reflect anomaly detection, and building out the report, AI knowledge and services for managing the data. My goal is a robust and realistic mock dataset.\n\n\n**Developing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI components, adding `reportService.ts` for report generation and downloads. The `aiService.ts` will handle natural language queries, delivering structured answers with context visualizations. I\'m also planning the `AppContext.tsx` for global state, and essential UI components like the Navbar, FloatingAIButton, ToastContainer, Badge, StatCard, Modal, and Empty component.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now deep in building out the UI components, focusing on crucial parts. I\'ve been creating components for loading states and empty states. I\'ve also been designing the interactive India Risk Map, using an SVG map for interactive state selections and risk levels, and implemented financial trend charts. The project card/table is in progress, as well as several modal components, including the new project modal, and an update status modal.\n\n\n**Mapping Page Structures**\n\nI\'m now mapping out page structures, ensuring they precisely match the provided screenshots. I\'m focusing on components like `EvidenceUploadModal`, and pages such as `DashboardPage`, `ProjectsPage`, `ProjectDetailPage`, `RiskAnalysisPage`, `MapPage`, `AIAssistantPage`, `ReportsPage`, and `SettingsPage`. I\'m going to create `src/types/index.ts` next to define my types.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 500617896
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
