    thinking: "**Generating Mock Data**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating realistic mock datasets. I\'m working on `src/data/mockProjects.ts`, `src/data/mockRiskClusters.ts`, `src/data/mockReports.ts`, and `src/data/mockStates.ts`. I\'m going to carefully verify the data against project screenshots to ensure accuracy, starting with `PRJ-20`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Project Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into detailed project data. I\'m taking a close look at a construction project in Ward 12, noting the budget, spending, and identified risks. The expenditure spike is a key area of concern, alongside the milestone delays. I am also reviewing the available evidence and identifying areas that require further scrutiny, such as missing plinth-level photos.\n\n\n**Examining Project Details**\n\nI\'m now closely examining specific project details, starting with those flagged for review. I\'m focusing on projects like the infrastructure project in Gorakhpur and the solar street lights in Baramati. I\'m noting the discrepancies between sanctioned amounts and spending, as well as the assigned risk levels. This is critical for identifying potential issues, particularly those with cost overruns or delays.\n\n\n"
