  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Detail**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting Screenshots 8, 9, and 10 to construct the Project Detail Page. Focusing on the top section, I\'ve identified the breadcrumbs/back bar, including the \"Back to Projects\" link and the project ID header (e.g., \"PRJ-2023-4921\"). Now, I\'m working to fully understand the components and styling needed for the rest of this section.\n\n\n**Defining Project Metrics**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the project\'s key metrics. I am now focused on the high-risk badge, ongoing status, and action buttons in the top right, as well as the crucial metrics: sanctioned amount, released funds, expenditure, and physical progress, with progress steps and risk assessment coming next. I\'m taking notes on these components.\n\n\n**Reviewing Severity Triggers**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the high-severity flag triggers for this project. Specifically, the material cost inflation and decoupled expenditure vs. physical progress are catching my attention. I\'ve also noted that the geotagged plinth proof for Tranche 2 is missing, which is a major red flag. I\'m carefully reviewing the specifics and implications of each of these issues.\n\n\n\n"
