  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the server design, initiating `GoogleGenAI` using the API key and User-Agent. My focus right now is on setting up an Express server and JSON body parsing. I\'m aiming for a straightforward and well-defined architecture.\n\n\n**Outlining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve specified API endpoints: `/api/gemini/chat` and `/api/gemini/grounded-query`. The chat endpoint handles multi-turn conversations with dynamic model selection and custom system instructions. The grounded query endpoint integrates search tools, returning extracted search chunks and URLs.\n\n\n**Expanding API Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating image and video generation endpoints. Specifically, I\'m implementing `/api/gemini/generate-image`, `/api/gemini/edit-image`, and `/api/gemini/generate-video`. The image endpoints leverage `gemini-3.1-flash` models. The video endpoint focuses on the `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview` model. My goal is to handle aspect ratios and base64 data conversion seamlessly. I plan to return relevant metadata for each request.\n\n\n**Defining Video Generation**\n\nI\'m expanding the API with video endpoints, covering aspect ratios (16:9, 9:16), resolutions (720p, 1080p), prompts, and optional base64 starting images. This involves `/api/gemini/video-status` for operation polling, `/api/gemini/video-download` to stream the completed video, and `/api/gemini/speech-briefing` for audio synthesis. I\'ve also added a health check endpoint at `/api/health` and a WebSocket server at `/ws/live` for real-time voice conversations. I\'m focused on setting up routes in `server.ts`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 65083468
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
