  planner_response {
    response: "I have integrated **Google Maps Grounding** powered by **Gemini 3.5 Flash** with the `googleMaps` tool across the application to ensure up-to-date and verified geospatial information.\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n- **Real-Time Google Maps Grounding**:\n  - Configured the grounding engine using `gemini-3.5-flash` and the `googleMaps` tool, with support for browser geolocation and explicit GPS coordinate binding (`retrievalConfig.latLng`).\n  - Extracted verified place titles and direct Google Maps destination links from `groundingChunks` to ensure full geospatial transparency and navigation routing.\n\n- **Dedicated GIS & Place Verification Hub**:\n  - Built an interactive Maps Grounding interface with preset queries for civic infrastructure (e.g., Primary Health Centers, municipal hospitals, schools, and collectorate offices).\n  - Implemented responsive cards displaying verified Google Maps places, direct navigation links, and Markdown-formatted spatial analysis.\n\n- **Deep Integration Across the Platform**:\n  - **Project Dossier**: Added a one-click Google Maps Grounding verification card directly beneath the constituency GIS cadastral map to cross-reference reported milestone coordinates against real-world terrain and civic landmarks.\n  - **Geographic Risk Map**: Enabled region-wide and project-level geospatial audit triggers to inspect surrounding facilities, road connectivity, and local points of interest.\n  - **Risk & Anomaly Queue**: Equipped the prioritization queue with instant Maps Grounding inspections to evaluate anomalous or geotag-mismatched works in real time."
    modified_response: "I have integrated **Google Maps Grounding** powered by **Gemini 3.5 Flash** with the `googleMaps` tool across the application to ensure up-to-date and verified geospatial information.\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n- **Real-Time Google Maps Grounding**:\n  - Configured the grounding engine using `gemini-3.5-flash` and the `googleMaps` tool, with support for browser geolocation and explicit GPS coordinate binding (`retrievalConfig.latLng`).\n  - Extracted verified place titles and direct Google Maps destination links from `groundingChunks` to ensure full geospatial transparency and navigation routing.\n\n- **Dedicated GIS & Place Verification Hub**:\n  - Built an interactive Maps Grounding interface with preset queries for civic infrastructure (e.g., Primary Health Centers, municipal hospitals, schools, and collectorate offices).\n  - Implemented responsive cards displaying verified Google Maps places, direct navigation links, and Markdown-formatted spatial analysis.\n\n- **Deep Integration Across the Platform**:\n  - **Project Dossier**: Added a one-click Google Maps Grounding verification card directly beneath the constituency GIS cadastral map to cross-reference reported milestone coordinates against real-world terrain and civic landmarks.\n  - **Geographic Risk Map**: Enabled region-wide and project-level geospatial audit triggers to inspect surrounding facilities, road connectivity, and local points of interest.\n  - **Risk & Anomaly Queue**: Equipped the prioritization queue with instant Maps Grounding inspections to evaluate anomalous or geotag-mismatched works in real time."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
